  "question": "Given that $\\vec{a} = 2\\hat{i} + \\hat{j} - \\hat{k}$, and $\\vec{b}$ is a unit vector such that $\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b} = 2$, find the angle $\\theta$ between $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$.",
  "answeroption": "A",
  "explanation": "$\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b} = |\\vec{a}|\\,|\\vec{b}| \\cos\\theta = 2$<br /><br />$|\\vec{a}| = \\sqrt{2^2 + 1^2 + (-1)^2} = \\sqrt{4+1+1} = \\sqrt{6}$<br /><br />$|\\vec{b}| = 1$<br /><br />So<br /><br />$\\sqrt{6} \\cos \\theta = 2$<br /><br />$\\cos \\theta = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}$<br /><br />$\\theta = \\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}\\right)$",
  "explanation_image": [],
